WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.470
Okay.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.420
I sort of alluded to this next question.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.660
The third audience question today is, David
does a middle ground on abortion exist?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.270
I heard you mentioned on the Joe Rogan program
that you can't include any crazy idea in the

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.650
discussion, but is there a middle ground on
the issue of abortion?

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.369
There is a middle ground on the issue of abortion
only when you've narrowed the conversation

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:21.609
in a pretty significant way.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:27.009
And what I mean by that is if your position
is abortion is murder and it should be illegal,

00:00:27.009 --> 00:00:31.439
I don't know how you find a middle ground
with that person that has any kind of legal

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:32.439
abortion.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:37.250
I mean the fundamentals of how different political
factions see abortion as an issue.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.190
A unfortunately prevent productive dialogue.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.490
And a lot of ways, my view is that this shouldn't
even be a discussion.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:52.970
There are lots of legal medical procedures
that if we see a video of may be repelling

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.350
in some way.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.950
This for me includes, you know, I don't want
to watch a heart bypass.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.790
I don't think it should be illegal.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.880
Doesn't mean I want to watch abortions, but
that doesn't mean those should be illegal.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:07.840
However, if you are brought to the table with
someone who says any abortion is murder because

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:14.620
um, you know, one day after conception that
is a person, I don't know how you actually

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.220
find a middle ground there.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.800
Now I do think that what's really different
about abortion than many other issues is the

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.070
outcome that the left and right at least claim
to want.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.900
And I believe do want is actually the same.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.909
The left and right both don't want abortions.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:36.830
So, so when you talk to the right, they don't
want abortion to be legal or accessible because

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.350
they believe that it is murder.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.930
When you talk to people on the left, they
don't want abortions to be necessary and they

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:49.180
want to reduce the number with sex education
and contraceptives and so on and so forth.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.130
But they do believe that abortion should be
legal and safe.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:58.780
That's why it's been so interesting to see
the resistance from the right to say, hey,

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.950
you know what?

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.979
The left actually does share the goal of reducing
the number of abortions.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:12.040
Empirical studies tell us how to do it and
it's with safe, uh, and, and legal, uh, safe

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.959
and full and inexpensive access to birth control
as well as comprehensive sex education.

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:18.959
They don't want that in.

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:23.140
A lot of this relates to what George Lakoff
describes as strict father morality where

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.540
it doesn't fit into the moral framework of
many on the right that you would be able to

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:36.250
have recreational, non procreative sex outside
of a marriage and have a tool that prevents

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.370
pregnancy.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:42.489
There's too many on the right who for moral
reasons believe that sex should be two different

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:47.530
degrees between married heterosexual couples
for the purposes of procreation.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:53.940
And if you do choose to have a sex outside
of marriage, then you don't deserve, it's

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.820
not right morally to have a way to prevent
a pregnancy because that would be chaos.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.220
And we know sort of all of the other beliefs
that come with that.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:08.340
Um, so the, the, the last thing I'll say on
this is the right has very successfully actually

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:14.251
manage the issue of abortion despite the fact
that over time the average position in the

00:03:14.251 --> 00:03:18.080
United States on abortion has moved towards,
I believe it should be legal in most cases,

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.080
more than half of the country.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:26.400
And I believe that when the right continues
to have these extreme positions sprinkled

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.349
in, at least any abortion should be illegal.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:33.849
These marches for life, right to life marches
where it gets completely wacky.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:37.069
I mean really, really wacky speeches and crazy
crazy stuff.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.310
They pull the Overton window to the right
and may benefit from this.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.310
That's the reality.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:46.860
It puts the pro choice contingent on having
to defend even abortion being being legal

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.870
rather than getting to the real issues of
providing contraception to people, sex, education,

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:51.870
et cetera.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.550
So unfortunately the Wright has succeeded
partially because they have used extreme positions

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.880
to pull the debate to the right, partially
because their framing is really simple.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.349
Abortion is murder and we shouldn't do it.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:05.520
Where's the position on the left is not abortions
all the time.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.599
No matter what.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:11.370
It's yes, we would like to reduce abortions,
but you have to take into consideration, uh,

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.159
all of these other factors, et Cetera, et
cetera.

00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:16.440
And George Lakoff has written a lot about
that as well.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.340
Uh, send me your thoughts.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:23.430
Is there something that we could call a middle
ground on abortion when one side of the debate

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:28.710
believes that any abortion is birth murder,
they should all be against the law and all

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:32.370
sorts of different people should be punished,
whether it's the doctors, the mothers, or

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.370
whoever else.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.370
Let me know what you think.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.650
We've got a great bonus show coming up for
you today.

